/**
\page documentation_guide Building and Browsing the Documentation

The README is the documentation's starting page. Its contents include the Composer library, command-line demo,
standalone server, and performance notes. Use **Guides** to jump directly to those sections.

## Where Should I Start?

| What You Want To Do | Where To Look |
| --- | --- |
| Install the library and make a lookup | [Composer Library](index.html#composer-library) and LGV_TZ_Lookup_Query. |
| Download current data and run a complete test | [Command-line Demo](index.html#turnkey-command-line-demo). |
| Run the HTTP service | [Standalone Server](index.html#standalone-server-implementation). |
| Understand storage and loading | LGV_TZ_Lookup_Database, LGV_TZ_Lookup_Entity, and LGV_TZ_Lookup_Loader. |
| Understand the independent demo checks | DemoSourceGeometry, DemoInspectingListener, and DemoTrackedDatabase. |
| Read implementation details | **API Reference** includes public/private members; **Source and Tests** includes annotated source. |
| Read release history | [CHANGELOG](../CHANGELOG.md). |

The source browser includes the package, HTTP entrypoint, demo, regression checks, and benchmark tools.
Downloaded boundary data and third-party vendor code are excluded from the documentation input.

## Generate the HTML

Run this from the project root:

\code{.sh}
./generate-docs.sh
\endcode

The script uses Doxygen from PATH, or the installed macOS Doxygen application. Set DOXYGEN to an executable path
if you use another installation. Graphviz's dot is optional; available installations add diagrams to the reference.

The output is written to docs/html. The script builds in a temporary directory first, then replaces old generated
output, so obsolete pages do not linger after source or filename changes. README images are copied with it,
and local links, images, scripts, styles, and HTML anchors are checked before the old output is replaced.

## Preview and GitHub Pages

For a local HTTP preview, run this from the project root:

\code{.sh}
python3 -m http.server 8000 --directory docs
\endcode

Open http://localhost:8000/. Browser search and navigation use static files and need no PHP server.

For GitHub Pages, commit the generated docs directory and select **Deploy from a branch**, with the publishing
folder set to `/docs`, in the repository's Pages settings. docs/index.html opens the generated landing page.
The .nojekyll marker keeps the generated files available as static documentation. See the
[GitHub Pages publishing instructions](https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/configuring-a-publishing-source-for-your-github-pages-site)
for the repository settings.

## Demo Command

